        {
            "Section": "IT.RPPERF",
            "Unnamed: 1": "RPPERF",
            "Unnamed: 2": "Was a reproductive system evaluation performed? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 1,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": "CL.C66742.NY.NY",
            "Unnamed: 7": 3,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "RPPERF [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "RPPERF [CDASH]\nIndicate whether or not a planned reproductive system evaluation was done. [completionInstructions]\nThis may be implemented for a series of reproductive system evaluations, or a specific reproductive system test. This general prompt question is used as a data management tool to verify that missing results are confirmed missing. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. May be used to derive a value into the SDTMIG variable RPSTAT. If the CDASH field RPPERF=\"N\", the value of RPSTAT will be \"NOT DONE\". If RPPERF=\"Y\", RPSTAT should be null. A combination of SDTMIG variables (e.g., RPCAT and RPSCAT, RPTPT) is used to indicate that multiple tests were not done. In this situation, the SDTMIG variable RPTESTCD would be populated as RPALL and an appropriate test name (RPTEST) provided. See SDTMIG v3.2 Section 4.1.5.1.2. [mappingInstructions]\nReproductive System Evaluation Performed [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.RPREASND",
